    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Make sure that the computer has at least 10 GB of free disk space. Make sure that the computer has a stable network connection. Save your open work.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Method 1: Wait, Then Restart",
      "body": "One update can need up to two hours on a slow network. If the message \"Getting updates\" does not change after 30 minutes, restart the computer.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Method 2: Run the Windows Update Troubleshooter",
      "body": "Windows Update includes a troubleshooter for common problems. Select Start > Settings > System > Troubleshoot…",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/how-to-fix-windows-11-stuck-on-getting-updates-loop/02-other-troubleshoot-windows-11.webp",
        "width": 1347,
        "height": 756
      },
      "durationInFrames": 343
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "kicker": "Code",
      "heading": "Method 3: Reset the Update Cache",
